00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.292
And I have to tell you,

00:00:01.292 --> 00:00:02.502
I have read everything

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:03.420
you've ever written.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.087
No, I mean it.

00:00:04.087 --> 00:00:05.964
I mean, when I read Euphoria at Midnight,

00:00:05.964 --> 00:00:07.716
all I wanted to do was become a writer.

00:00:07.716 --> 00:00:08.675
Oh, please, honey.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:08.967
Listen,

00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:10.385
if I can do it, anybody

00:00:10.385 --> 00:00:11.803
can you just start with

00:00:11.803 --> 00:00:13.471
half a dozen European cities,

00:00:13.471 --> 00:00:14.889
throw in 30 euphemisms

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:16.850
for male genitalia, and bam,

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:20.061
You have got yourself a book.

00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:21.146
My mother.

00:00:21.146 --> 00:00:23.732
Ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:23.732 --> 00:00:25.066
I was actor Matthew Perry

00:00:25.066 --> 00:00:26.026
and his iconic role

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.402
as Chandler Bing on Friends.

00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:29.154
The beloved actor was found dead

00:00:29.154 --> 00:00:31.197
in a hot tub at his home

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.074
in Los Angeles on Saturday.

00:00:33.074 --> 00:00:34.659
A law enforcement source tells CNN

00:00:34.659 --> 00:00:36.494
there is no foul play suspected.

00:00:36.494 --> 00:00:38.496
Perry's death is under investigation.

00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:39.456
Perry landed several high

00:00:39.456 --> 00:00:40.206
profile TV

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.042
roles and movies in movies

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.543
and TV shows like Beverly Hills,

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:45.211
92 on Oth throughout his career.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.921
But it was his unforgettable

00:00:46.921 --> 00:00:48.381
role as Chandler Bing

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:49.841
that made him a household name.

00:00:49.841 --> 00:00:51.009
The creators of Friends

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:52.302
released a statement saying, quote,

00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:53.094
He was always

00:00:53.094 --> 00:00:54.637
the funniest person in the room.

00:00:54.637 --> 00:00:55.305
More than that,

00:00:55.305 --> 00:00:56.347
he was the sweetest

00:00:56.347 --> 00:00:58.558
with a giving and selfless heart.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:00:59.559
Joining us now from Kansas

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:00.143
City, Missouri,

00:01:00.143 --> 00:01:01.311
where she's been appearing

00:01:01.311 --> 00:01:02.896
in always a bridesmaid

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:04.147
at the new theater is actress

00:01:04.147 --> 00:01:04.981
Morgan Fairchild,

00:01:04.981 --> 00:01:07.317
who you just saw played Matthew Perry's

00:01:07.317 --> 00:01:09.527
TV mom and friends.

00:01:09.527 --> 00:01:11.112
Thanks so much for joining us.

00:01:11.112 --> 00:01:14.115
There's an unlimited number of clips

00:01:14.199 --> 00:01:15.533
that you want to show

00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:16.409
and you want to laugh at

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.160
and you want to be a part of.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.787
But I want to start with

00:01:18.787 --> 00:01:19.871
how would you remember

00:01:19.871 --> 00:01:20.789
you said you were heartbroken.

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:24.793
How do you remember working with Matthew?

00:01:24.876 --> 00:01:25.794
You know,

00:01:25.794 --> 00:01:27.796
I just always remember Matthew

00:01:27.796 --> 00:01:31.800
as from the first day on the set and

00:01:31.883 --> 00:01:33.635
the show was not a huge hit yet

00:01:33.635 --> 00:01:35.345
when I started working on it

00:01:35.345 --> 00:01:37.222
and he came bounding over to me

00:01:37.222 --> 00:01:39.557
and I literally bounding like a big puppy

00:01:39.557 --> 00:01:40.725
and said, Oh,

00:01:40.725 --> 00:01:41.935
you won't remember me,

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.478
but I used to visit you

00:01:43.478 --> 00:01:44.687
on the set of Flamingo Road

00:01:44.687 --> 00:01:46.523
and Falcon Crest with my dad.

00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:48.191
And I said, Oh, who is your dad?

00:01:48.191 --> 00:01:49.400
He said, John Bennett Perry.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:49.692
I said,

00:01:49.692 --> 00:01:51.277
Oh my God, you're that little kid.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:52.987
It's like, Oh, okay.

00:01:52.987 --> 00:01:55.031
And so right from the first

00:01:55.031 --> 00:01:57.700
there was just that ebullience, that joy,

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:59.619
that kind of a friendly

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:00.787
and wonderful,

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.080
acerbic, but

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:05.083
puppy dog kind of feel about Matthew.

00:02:05.083 --> 00:02:07.001
He was such a warm and

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:10.505
wonderful and funny and

00:02:10.588 --> 00:02:13.133
creative young man.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:13.508
You know,

00:02:13.508 --> 00:02:15.218
I was looking at some of the pictures

00:02:15.218 --> 00:02:16.219
over the weekend of us

00:02:16.219 --> 00:02:17.137
and realized, oh, my God,

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:19.514
this is almost 30 years ago. Yeah.

00:02:19.514 --> 00:02:21.141
So we've all grown up together.

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:23.518
The audience has grown up with Matt

00:02:23.518 --> 00:02:24.853
as their best friend,

00:02:24.853 --> 00:02:25.353
the person

00:02:25.353 --> 00:02:26.646
they wanted to be, the person

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.356
they wanted to meet, to know

00:02:28.356 --> 00:02:29.649
and have as a friend.

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:32.902
And we all kind of grew up together

00:02:32.902 --> 00:02:33.736
with me.

00:02:33.736 --> 00:02:36.739
Me being his fake mom.

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:37.532
Was so interesting.

00:02:37.532 --> 00:02:38.449
We for years

00:02:38.449 --> 00:02:40.618
watching friends saw

00:02:40.618 --> 00:02:42.453
what he showed the world, right?

00:02:42.453 --> 00:02:43.454
How funny he was,

00:02:43.454 --> 00:02:45.540
what a great actor he was.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:46.916
But then later in life,

00:02:46.916 --> 00:02:47.834
when he wrote his book

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:48.459
and he came out

00:02:48.459 --> 00:02:50.086
to talk about his addiction

00:02:50.086 --> 00:02:51.379
and his struggles,

00:02:51.379 --> 00:02:54.465
we also saw his reality and his humanity

00:02:54.465 --> 00:02:55.091
and everything

00:02:55.091 --> 00:02:56.176
that he has dealt with that

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:58.094
so many people could relate to.

00:02:58.094 --> 00:02:59.179
And I just was moved.

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:00.638
MORGAN When he said, you know,

00:03:00.638 --> 00:03:01.139
I want to be

00:03:01.139 --> 00:03:02.056
someone who people

00:03:02.056 --> 00:03:03.224
can come up on the street

00:03:03.224 --> 00:03:05.435
and ask for help and I can help them.

00:03:05.435 --> 00:03:06.561
And he wanted his legacy

00:03:06.561 --> 00:03:07.520
to be a lot about that

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.149
and not just acting

00:03:11.232 --> 00:03:11.649
well.

00:03:11.649 --> 00:03:12.609
And I think that

00:03:12.609 --> 00:03:13.610
was one of the very,

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:17.238
very special things about Matthew.

00:03:17.322 --> 00:03:19.324
I watched him go from a young man

00:03:19.324 --> 00:03:20.617
and he was 23, 24

00:03:20.617 --> 00:03:22.410
when we started working together

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:25.038
and obviously had some issues

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:27.665
during the time he was on Friends.

00:03:27.665 --> 00:03:29.000
I never saw it on the set.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.002
He was always very professional.

00:03:31.002 --> 00:03:32.921
But then when you started hearing

00:03:32.921 --> 00:03:33.880
about some of the things

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.048
he had gone through,

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:36.799
I think one of the bravest things

00:03:36.799 --> 00:03:38.635
that he did in his career

00:03:38.635 --> 00:03:41.012
and his life was to go public,

00:03:41.012 --> 00:03:42.138
to write this book,

00:03:42.138 --> 00:03:43.806
to reach out to other people,

00:03:43.806 --> 00:03:46.226
to try to be of help, to other people.

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:47.560
And that was one of the most

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.854
endearing things about him,

00:03:49.854 --> 00:03:52.232
is that, as they said in the intro,

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.107
not only was

00:03:53.107 --> 00:03:55.526
he always the funniest guy in the room

00:03:55.526 --> 00:03:59.113
and the quickest wit and the most happy

00:03:59.113 --> 00:04:00.823
and up seemingly,

00:04:00.823 --> 00:04:03.326
but also one of the kindest

00:04:03.326 --> 00:04:07.080
and having having had friends and family

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.206
with addiction problems

00:04:08.206 --> 00:04:10.458
in my life, people that I cared about.

00:04:10.458 --> 00:04:11.292
I know

00:04:11.292 --> 00:04:13.086
how hard that is for the addict

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:15.421
and also for the people who love them.

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:16.839
And I thought it was terribly

00:04:16.839 --> 00:04:20.260
brave of him to want that

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:23.263
to be part of his legacy as a human being

00:04:23.388 --> 00:04:25.390
is not only the joy that he brought

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:27.100
to people, the great acting,

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.768
the great fun parts,

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:31.229
but also the reaching out

00:04:31.229 --> 00:04:32.188
to trying to help

00:04:32.188 --> 00:04:33.189
other people,

00:04:33.189 --> 00:04:34.899
the being honest about what

00:04:34.899 --> 00:04:36.150
he was facing in life.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:37.068
Because to me,

00:04:37.068 --> 00:04:38.444
that's what we're all really here

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:39.696
for, is to help each other

00:04:39.696 --> 00:04:40.905
get through this.

00:04:40.905 --> 00:04:43.199
And he was doing that big time.

00:04:43.199 --> 00:04:44.450
That's really beautifully said.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.451
It would mean a lot to him.

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:46.828
MORGAN, I'm sure.

00:04:46.828 --> 00:04:47.203
Can I ask

00:04:47.203 --> 00:04:48.037
before we let you go,

00:04:48.037 --> 00:04:50.498
what made him so good at his job?

00:04:50.498 --> 00:04:51.833
You mentioned that you never saw

00:04:51.833 --> 00:04:53.042
any issues on set.

00:04:53.042 --> 00:04:53.584
He was always

00:04:53.584 --> 00:04:54.377
the funniest guy in the room.

00:04:54.377 --> 00:04:55.336
His delivery.

00:04:55.336 --> 00:04:56.587
I don't think you could mimic it

00:04:56.587 --> 00:04:58.256
if you tried to study it for years.

00:04:58.256 --> 00:04:59.716
What made him so great?

00:04:59.716 --> 00:05:01.884
Okay. Okay. Go to work.

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:02.552
Well, you

00:05:02.552 --> 00:05:03.970
know, I mean, I've gotten to work

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.805
with a few wonderful comics.

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:06.472
You know, Robin

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.891
Williams being one of them.

00:05:08.891 --> 00:05:12.020
And he had that magnificent quality of

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:13.813
just being so quick,

00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:16.566
so smart, so quick and that quick turn

00:05:16.566 --> 00:05:19.444
and he could he could just pop up

00:05:19.444 --> 00:05:19.986
with something

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:20.653
that you were not

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:22.488
expecting out of the blue.

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:23.573
And it made it work,

00:05:23.573 --> 00:05:25.116
especially when we're working together

00:05:25.116 --> 00:05:26.492
with this sort of weird

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:27.368
mother son

00:05:27.368 --> 00:05:28.911
relationship that Chandler

00:05:28.911 --> 00:05:29.662
and Nora

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:31.748
being had where he was always

00:05:31.748 --> 00:05:32.623
so embarrassed

00:05:32.623 --> 00:05:33.458
by her

00:05:33.458 --> 00:05:35.043
and part of his neuroses,

00:05:35.043 --> 00:05:36.669
trying to deal with his parents,

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.921
which I think a lot of kids could

00:05:38.921 --> 00:05:40.423
identify with.

00:05:40.423 --> 00:05:41.841
But he was just always so quick,

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:43.843
Just so quick

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:45.094
and in real life, too.

00:05:45.094 --> 00:05:46.721
Very funny, very witty.

00:05:46.721 --> 00:05:49.307
And it affected it affected his acting.

00:05:49.307 --> 00:05:52.560
His acting showed that that quick turn

00:05:52.643 --> 00:05:54.187
that cut you off guard, that

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:56.606
that made you laugh because he was

00:05:56.606 --> 00:05:59.359
he was just a very endearing, fun,

00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:01.152
wonderful, wonderful guy.

00:06:01.152 --> 00:06:02.612
And I send my love

00:06:02.612 --> 00:06:05.281
and condolences to his family.

00:06:05.281 --> 00:06:07.992
I just felt that I should do something

00:06:07.992 --> 00:06:09.911
because for millions of people

00:06:09.911 --> 00:06:11.412
who watch the show, they

00:06:11.412 --> 00:06:12.747
they sometimes think of me

00:06:12.747 --> 00:06:15.166
as his mom, as Chandler's mom,

00:06:15.166 --> 00:06:17.001
and I just I just

00:06:17.001 --> 00:06:18.336
I just wanted to reach out

00:06:18.336 --> 00:06:20.213
because I've gotten lots of condolences

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:22.173
on social media from all over the world.

00:06:22.173 --> 00:06:23.383
You realize how many

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:24.300
how many people

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.426
this show touched,

00:06:25.426 --> 00:06:26.552
how many people felt that

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.513
it helped them grow up,

00:06:28.513 --> 00:06:30.390
that they identified with this character,

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:31.557
wanting to be the character,

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:32.517
be the best friend,

00:06:32.517 --> 00:06:35.645
and just as his fake mom,

00:06:35.645 --> 00:06:37.939
I just want to say how much I loved him

00:06:37.939 --> 00:06:39.857
and how special he was

00:06:39.857 --> 00:06:42.860
and and thank you to

00:06:42.944 --> 00:06:43.361
let his

00:06:43.361 --> 00:06:44.946
family know all the condolences

00:06:44.946 --> 00:06:47.490
I have gotten to pass on to them.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:48.950
So glad you joined

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:49.909
us, Morgan, this morning

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:51.369
for all those great memories.

00:06:51.369 --> 00:06:53.621
Thanks very much.

00:06:53.621 --> 00:06:54.997
Thank you. Thank you.

